5. Important Notes Before Running
Paper trade first. Change PORT = 7497 in myIBApp.py to use the TWS paper account; leave dry_run=True for a first pass that only logs the trades without sending them.
Exchange routing. myIBApp.make_stock_contract hardcodes NASDAQ. SPY/QQQ route via ARCA, most NYSE names via SMART. I override it with self.contract.exchange = cfg.exchange in the strategy — use "SMART" if you're unsure.
Bar granularity. reqRealTimeBars only supports 5-second bars. If you want to trade on 1-minute or 5-minute bars, aggregate 5-sec bars in on_bar (or poll fetch_historical on a timer for longer timeframes).
Stationarity filter. The default requires ADF p<0.05 AND half-life in [1, 30] bars. SPY daily prices will almost always fail this (they trend). This is intentional — the "right" mean-reversion setup is usually on a spread between two cointegrated ETFs (e.g., XLF/KRE). Set require_stationary=False to trade anyway during development.
Pairs extension. To convert to pairs trading, fetch both series, regress A on B to get β, feed spread_t = A − β·B into self.prices, and submit two simultaneous orders in _enter_long/_enter_short (buy A / short β·B, etc.).
Commissions & slippage. The live system uses MKT orders for simplicity; for production, prefer marketable limit orders and include commission/slippage assumptions when backtesting. 
