6. Quick Smoke Test
Start TWS in paper mode, enable the API (Global Config → API → Enable ActiveX and Socket Clients), port 7497.
Set PORT = 7497 in myIBApp.py and cfg.dry_run = True in mean_reversion.py.
Run python mean_reversion.py.
You should see: connection log → warm-up ADF/half-life/Hurst stats → "Subscribed to real-time bars" → z-score-driven entry/exit lines as new bars arrive.
Once comfortable, flip dry_run=False to send real (paper) orders.
This gives you a full end-to-end mean-reversion bot: data in, signal computed, risk sized, orders sent, positions tracked, and shutdown-safe. From here you can layer on logging-to-CSV, a proper backtest harness, and the pairs-trading variant.
